WEBVTT

01:10.050 --> 01:11.840
I got what you asked for.

01:13.990 --> 01:15.840
What are you trying to do?

01:23.360 --> 01:24.410
What's that?

01:46.660 --> 01:50.200
<i>My tears scattered like bits of paper</i>

01:50.200 --> 01:53.910
<i>Scared of the unknowable tomorrow</i>

01:53.910 --> 01:57.430
<i>I lived the same day over and over,
 back and forth</i>

01:57.430 --> 02:01.260
<i>But a new morning never came</i>

02:01.260 --> 02:03.510
<i>All the reasons to calm down</i>

02:03.510 --> 02:07.940
<i>Are just some moments until the crash</i>

02:08.460 --> 02:11.440
<i>I'm no longer the one that everyone knows</i>

02:11.440 --> 02:15.740
<i>Took off the fragile armor</i>

02:15.740 --> 02:22.810
<i>I don't want to lose any more love</i>

02:23.230 --> 02:30.290
<i>I don't want to lose any more love</i>

02:30.290 --> 02:33.980
<i>There's still no line 
between today and tomorrow</i>

02:33.980 --> 02:37.550
<i>My waking nightmare doesn't end</i>

02:37.550 --> 02:41.180
<i>And yet I won't lose hope</i>

02:41.180 --> 02:47.230
<i>And yet there's no night that doesn't end</i>

02:47.230 --> 02:59.570
<i>Not here, not here</i>

03:11.020 --> 03:12.390
What is this?

03:13.920 --> 03:15.550
We've hit the production limit.

03:16.900 --> 03:19.040
They put too great a load on the plants.

03:20.070 --> 03:23.260
It cut them off from the higher dimension.

03:23.910 --> 03:25.800
They can't maintain their bodies.

03:27.330 --> 03:29.270
They're already in the terminal stage...

03:39.390 --> 03:40.900
What are you doing?

03:40.900 --> 03:42.860
This area is off-limits.

03:43.370 --> 03:47.440
What are you doing?! Why did you continue 
to overload them beyond the threshold?

03:47.440 --> 03:48.740
As if they're disposable?!

03:48.740 --> 03:51.540
Isn't it obvious? 
To speed up the reconstruction.

03:51.540 --> 03:55.010
It's the only way we can hope 
to prosper on this planet.

03:55.010 --> 03:57.960
Now leave. Their Last Run will start soon.

03:58.600 --> 03:59.910
"Last Run"?

04:00.630 --> 04:01.800
Let's go.

04:02.420 --> 04:04.010
Heal them.

04:04.010 --> 04:05.760
Heal them now, Doctor!

04:07.980 --> 04:09.640
It's too late...

04:13.020 --> 04:14.650
This is it.

04:16.660 --> 04:18.420
The Last Run...

04:18.420 --> 04:23.040
When you force a plant that's reached its 
production limit to go out of control,

04:23.040 --> 04:25.030
it uses up all of its remaining energy.

04:25.030 --> 04:27.020
One final harvest.

04:50.360 --> 04:53.180
I'm sorry. Please forgive us...

04:54.380 --> 04:56.280
Forgive us humans.

05:01.170 --> 05:01.980
Nai...

05:20.770 --> 05:22.480
I knew you were alive.

05:23.200 --> 05:27.460
Vash, you must have heard them.

05:27.460 --> 05:29.420
Their screams.

05:30.850 --> 05:34.850
Now you know. 
<i>This</i> is the true nature of humanity.

05:36.720 --> 05:39.570
They're born to serve us humans.

05:39.570 --> 05:42.150
I'm sure they were happy to be useful.

05:43.340 --> 05:46.860
Now, we're busy here.

05:46.860 --> 05:49.140
I'll have to ask you outsiders to leave.

05:50.660 --> 05:51.620
Hurry it up.

05:51.620 --> 05:53.990
Stop! Don't touch him!

05:56.300 --> 05:58.830
Didn't you hear them?

05:58.830 --> 06:01.440
Their dying cries?!

06:05.860 --> 06:09.600
If so, there's no need for words...

06:11.150 --> 06:12.810
Just let me hear your screams.

06:16.140 --> 06:17.020
Shit!

06:21.950 --> 06:23.680
Stop this, Nai!

06:26.470 --> 06:27.660
"Nai," huh?

06:29.140 --> 06:31.370
I haven't heard that name in a long time.

06:32.270 --> 06:37.210
I now represent my myriad of brethren
 spread across the planet.

06:37.210 --> 06:39.870
I shall cut down humanity in their stead.

06:41.360 --> 06:43.460
I am Millions Knives.

06:55.520 --> 06:58.390
Why? Why did you kill them?

06:59.240 --> 07:01.940
Rem sacrificed herself to save these people!

07:01.940 --> 07:06.280
That's right. If it weren't for her meddling,

07:06.820 --> 07:10.830
every ship other than the plant carriers
 would've been rubble.

07:12.450 --> 07:18.530
After all the work I did to swap out 
the navigation data for every single ship...

07:21.650 --> 07:23.460
Get them!

07:23.460 --> 07:24.570
Don't move!

07:25.360 --> 07:29.300
Vash... Let's build a paradise together.

07:29.770 --> 07:34.510
Free our brethren from the foul humans.

07:34.510 --> 07:38.710
Plants can't survive without 
humans to take care of them.

07:38.710 --> 07:40.140
Remember what Rem said?

07:40.530 --> 07:46.190
Outside of human control, plants use up 
all their energy in one burst and die.

07:46.190 --> 07:49.530
So you bought into that nonsense...

07:50.350 --> 07:54.290
No matter how comfortable, 
chains are still chains.

07:54.290 --> 07:56.120
But we're different.

07:56.120 --> 07:59.290
You and I have our own will, 
and we walk freely.

07:59.290 --> 08:01.540
<i>This</i> is power!

08:08.540 --> 08:11.280
We had to do this to survive—

08:26.610 --> 08:30.820
An evil weapon of the Sinners, 
taking lives easily from afar

08:30.820 --> 08:33.860
with the twitch of a finger...

08:34.570 --> 08:37.920
A fitting arm for a human-lover like you.

08:39.450 --> 08:42.550
The plants are the ones who need power.

08:43.160 --> 08:47.790
I have what we need. 
Now all you and I need to do is proceed.

08:49.000 --> 08:50.950
What are you planning?

08:53.500 --> 08:54.650
Vash!

08:55.830 --> 08:56.900
Luida!

08:57.460 --> 08:59.100
What are you doing here?

08:59.100 --> 09:02.180
I came to get you. Let's go home together.

09:05.410 --> 09:08.190
What a great opportunity. Take aim, Vash.

09:08.550 --> 09:11.250
Kill her as your first step.

09:12.360 --> 09:13.850
Everyone's waiting for you.

09:15.070 --> 09:16.290
Vash!

09:17.710 --> 09:20.590
What's wrong? Do it already.

09:27.380 --> 09:30.630
You really can't do anything without me.

09:39.610 --> 09:40.720
Nai!

09:46.500 --> 09:50.610
Until the bitter end,
 all I did was let Rem protect me!

09:51.050 --> 09:54.350
Because of that, I lost her!

09:54.840 --> 09:59.410
So I won't let you take
 anyone else away from me!

09:59.870 --> 10:01.980
Vash!

10:05.050 --> 10:06.410
You witch...

10:08.260 --> 10:09.670
How many times?

10:10.820 --> 10:14.780
How many times will you steal him from me?

10:18.050 --> 10:20.300
Stop...

10:22.230 --> 10:23.180
Stop this.

10:27.980 --> 10:29.770
Wh-What's that?!

10:35.190 --> 10:36.370
What...

10:38.430 --> 10:39.520
is this?

10:50.390 --> 10:51.380
You fool!

10:52.090 --> 10:54.140
Is that... a gate?

11:16.290 --> 11:17.280
Vash!

11:17.280 --> 11:18.150
Don't touch him!

11:20.790 --> 11:24.130
Don't touch Vash!

11:37.740 --> 11:42.300
Just wait for a short while... 
A mere century or so.

11:43.070 --> 11:46.250
I promise I'll build a world of plants.

11:56.540 --> 11:59.240
Vash! Vash!

12:00.660 --> 12:01.840
Vash!

12:20.050 --> 12:23.640
Hey, Vash. Heard you busted your arm again.

12:23.640 --> 12:24.880
Brad...

12:26.460 --> 12:30.170
Every time you come back, 
you've messed up my masterpiece.

12:30.170 --> 12:32.580
I, uh... don't have anything
 to say for myself.

12:32.580 --> 12:34.390
Come on. Show it to me.

12:37.350 --> 12:39.440
You never change, Brad.

12:39.440 --> 12:41.490
Look who's talking.

12:41.490 --> 12:44.560
Forever young... I'm jealous.

12:46.260 --> 12:48.450
Come on. Stay still.

12:53.370 --> 12:54.790
Welcome back.

12:57.180 --> 12:58.420
I'm home.

12:59.210 --> 13:00.420
What about the others?

13:00.990 --> 13:06.380
They're safe. Everyone from the Sand Steamer,
 the orphanage, and your friends.

13:06.380 --> 13:07.860
My friends?

13:09.720 --> 13:11.180
Vash!

13:11.180 --> 13:12.490
Sheesh.

13:12.490 --> 13:14.480
Who said anything about being friends?

13:15.140 --> 13:16.950
Thank you.

13:16.950 --> 13:19.480
You're the reason we managed to stop the ship.

13:19.830 --> 13:24.770
Who'd've thought there was a spaceship
 hiding here in the sandstorm, though?

13:25.180 --> 13:27.560
Think of it as a form of camouflage.

13:28.270 --> 13:29.990
You folks really saved us.

13:31.490 --> 13:35.030
Have you two known Vash for a long time?

13:35.030 --> 13:38.440
Yeah, you could say that.
 About 150 years, I guess.

13:39.230 --> 13:40.240
What?!

13:40.240 --> 13:41.710
A century and a half?!

13:42.420 --> 13:44.390
Cold sleep.

13:44.390 --> 13:47.200
We don't age during that time.

13:48.520 --> 13:53.430
We have to maintain this ship 
for as long as possible.

13:54.250 --> 13:58.720
To that end, many of 
the passengers are still asleep.

13:59.440 --> 14:02.730
Oh. So it's not eternal life.

14:02.730 --> 14:04.010
Of course not.

14:04.010 --> 14:08.200
We're only human. Although we have
 a little help from technology.

14:09.590 --> 14:12.410
And from plants?

14:17.190 --> 14:19.010
Let me show you something.

14:24.550 --> 14:26.820
Wow!

14:33.920 --> 14:37.180
Incredible... What is this place?

14:40.880 --> 14:42.730
So much beautiful green!

14:43.280 --> 14:45.650
Well, color me surprised.

14:45.650 --> 14:48.360
Roberto! Come here, come here!

14:49.380 --> 14:50.770
Now, now...

14:51.220 --> 14:52.920
Ouch...

14:54.990 --> 14:56.200
What are these?

14:56.980 --> 14:58.860
These are flora.

14:58.860 --> 15:00.080
Flora?

15:00.080 --> 15:03.340
They grow using photosynthesis and multiply.

15:03.340 --> 15:06.600
They're a life-form that is 
neither human nor Worm.

15:07.270 --> 15:08.590
They're alive?

15:09.500 --> 15:14.850
They're made of not just water,
but nutrients as well.

15:14.850 --> 15:17.260
So if we just make more of these...

15:18.250 --> 15:20.230
Is it that simple?

15:20.690 --> 15:23.950
This dome must be supported by plants.

15:24.710 --> 15:27.070
And not just one or two.

15:27.070 --> 15:31.310
But the flora can lessen 
the load on the plants.

15:32.060 --> 15:36.360
Given time, we can spread the
 greenery across the entire planet.

15:36.360 --> 15:41.250
Yeah? And how long is that going to take?
Decades? Centuries?

15:41.840 --> 15:46.710
No matter how long it takes, 
I want to follow the right path.

15:47.170 --> 15:51.270
I don't want to justify 
wrongdoing just to survive.

15:53.060 --> 15:55.620
You sound like Vash.

15:55.620 --> 15:57.720
"The right path"? Jeez...

15:58.910 --> 16:02.970
There's no place for niceties on this planet.

16:03.600 --> 16:06.200
I don't care for your way of thinking.

16:07.180 --> 16:11.380
But you're free to go your own way.

16:11.380 --> 16:12.980
And I'll go mine.

16:12.980 --> 16:15.700
I just hope we're headed for the same goal.

16:16.190 --> 16:18.700
There's one thing I need to tell you.

16:18.700 --> 16:19.740
What?

16:20.130 --> 16:21.940
No smoking on the ship.

16:24.770 --> 16:27.770
Right after he sounded so cool for once...

16:27.770 --> 16:31.760
Meryl! Go find somewhere I can smoke!

16:31.760 --> 16:34.330
Yeah, yeah. Or you could do it yourself—

16:38.220 --> 16:42.000
Roberto! Did you just call me "Meryl"?

16:42.000 --> 16:43.480
You finally said my name!

16:43.480 --> 16:45.650
Huh? Did I?

16:45.650 --> 16:46.630
You did!

16:46.630 --> 16:47.980
I don't believe it.

16:47.980 --> 16:50.730
What do you mean? You just said it!

16:50.730 --> 16:51.850
Didn't happen.

16:51.850 --> 16:54.950
Come on! Say it again!

16:52.550 --> 16:54.950
Didn't happen! Didn't happen! Didn't happen!

16:56.650 --> 17:01.740
Okay, Needle-noggin...
I got something to ask you.

17:01.740 --> 17:02.700
Hm?

17:03.190 --> 17:04.730
You don't, by any chance,

17:04.730 --> 17:08.710
think you can make up with 
Millions Knives, do you?

17:12.460 --> 17:14.100
C'mon, Needle-noggin...

17:14.100 --> 17:15.270
I won't kill.

17:16.240 --> 17:19.390
I will never kill anyone again.

17:20.370 --> 17:22.720
I'll find a way to save them all...

17:23.740 --> 17:27.560
The humans, the plants, and Nai.

17:28.810 --> 17:30.980
More empty words.

17:31.560 --> 17:35.800
I swear to you the day will come 
when you have to pick between them.

17:36.510 --> 17:38.410
You're just like how I used to be.

17:38.410 --> 17:39.160
Huh?

17:39.160 --> 17:44.790
Trying to bite Vash's head off, 
thinking everything's all black and white.

17:44.790 --> 17:47.540
I was like that as a young one.

17:47.540 --> 17:50.290
Big talk, old man.

17:51.210 --> 17:53.440
Vash is tough.

17:53.440 --> 17:56.270
You'll learn that yourself if you hang around.

17:58.930 --> 18:00.130
Luida!

18:00.760 --> 18:02.380
A swarm of Worms...

18:06.540 --> 18:07.570
Is this...

18:08.580 --> 18:09.580
Look.

18:11.660 --> 18:14.550
It's Zazie. No doubt about it.

18:25.170 --> 18:27.780
Where are we?

18:30.200 --> 18:33.540
Roberto! Wake up, Roberto!

18:37.130 --> 18:40.240
Hm? It's night already?

18:40.240 --> 18:41.690
Are you okay?

18:42.270 --> 18:45.450
Hey there, newbie. You good?

18:46.640 --> 18:49.900
So... where are we?

18:50.510 --> 18:51.520
I don't know.

18:52.310 --> 18:54.330
A smoking area, maybe?

18:54.330 --> 18:56.270
Keep dreaming.

18:56.270 --> 18:59.450
Welcome to the third of the seven cities.

19:00.500 --> 19:04.330
This is JuLai, a crashed plant carrier.

19:04.330 --> 19:06.740
You there... Have we met?

19:06.740 --> 19:10.830
Oh, right, you haven't seen me 
in this outfit before.

19:11.420 --> 19:13.350
Did Knives send you?

19:13.350 --> 19:14.130
Huh?

19:14.130 --> 19:16.910
Let's talk about something more interesting.

19:17.360 --> 19:23.000
This planet you call Noman's Land 
now stands at a crossroads.

19:24.460 --> 19:26.510
So I want to find out...

19:26.510 --> 19:31.810
Who do we Worms side with? 
You humans? Or the plants?

19:36.280 --> 19:37.820
It's no use.

19:38.620 --> 19:41.600
This body is just a conduit.

19:41.600 --> 19:46.000
Who are you to make such a grand judgment?

19:46.540 --> 19:48.880
This is <i>our</i> planet.

19:49.390 --> 19:51.250
We were here long before you came.

19:52.440 --> 19:55.790
Besides, you're repeat offenders.

19:56.160 --> 19:57.350
"Repeat offenders"?

20:05.210 --> 20:10.390
You humans messed up your 
home planet, Earth, right?

20:10.780 --> 20:13.830
That's why you sent colony ships
 to this new planet.

20:14.430 --> 20:16.860
What? That can't be...

20:17.330 --> 20:18.520
It's true.

20:33.210 --> 20:37.960
Earth used to be a lush place 
of bountiful resources.

20:38.490 --> 20:41.890
It was full of life, and not just human.

20:43.090 --> 20:44.230
But...

20:47.170 --> 20:50.270
You humans gobbled it all up.

20:54.080 --> 20:56.770
That's a lie.

20:57.240 --> 21:00.230
Why do you think the colony ships crashed?

21:00.820 --> 21:02.940
Those twins did it.

21:02.940 --> 21:03.830
Twins?

21:03.830 --> 21:05.490
That's crazy talk.

21:05.490 --> 21:08.630
Do you mean Vash?

21:08.630 --> 21:12.250
What has he been doing in the
 century and a half since the crash?

21:14.250 --> 21:18.460
Maybe for plants,
 a century and a half is nothing.

21:32.350 --> 21:33.270
These are...

21:33.830 --> 21:36.670
Knives brought them here from all over.

21:36.670 --> 21:38.370
Knives did?

21:38.370 --> 21:39.740
What are you doing?

21:41.170 --> 21:44.220
Whoops, he's discovered us.

21:44.220 --> 21:45.990
So it's you, the Beast.

21:47.020 --> 21:49.070
Why did you bring them here?

21:49.070 --> 21:50.990
I don't take orders from you.

21:51.690 --> 21:54.860
Knives accepted me as a guest.

21:55.550 --> 21:57.250
Please tell me!

21:57.250 --> 21:59.580
Why collect the red plants?

22:00.020 --> 22:01.900
You don't need to know.

22:03.150 --> 22:08.010
I'll tell you.
But you have to tell me in return...

22:09.570 --> 22:12.010
Who will benefit this planet more? Humans?

22:12.370 --> 22:13.980
Or plants?

22:16.230 --> 22:20.020
Which do you think?

22:20.020 --> 22:27.640
<i>Your light...</i>

22:34.100 --> 22:38.400
<i>If that light never changes</i>

22:38.400 --> 22:42.830
<i>And continues to shine high above the sky</i>

22:42.830 --> 22:47.140
<i>Even when I'm lost, 
even when I'm struggling</i>

22:47.140 --> 22:51.390
<i>I'll continue to search for you</i>

22:51.390 --> 22:55.680
<i>Even on days of sickness or sadness</i>

22:55.680 --> 23:00.060
<i>I'll open the window to a new morning</i>

23:00.060 --> 23:04.250
<i>I'm moving forward, I'm standing still</i>

23:04.250 --> 23:07.810
<i>Tell the people who are praying</i>

23:07.810 --> 23:13.770
<i>But today this flower 
before me is praising you</i>

23:13.770 --> 23:16.780
<i>My song is a song of joy and wishes</i>

23:16.780 --> 23:19.500
<i>Yes, I'm reaching out</i>

23:19.500 --> 23:24.840
<i>But you're too high up 
in the evening stars</i>

23:24.840 --> 23:30.810
<i>But today this flower 
before me is praising you</i>

23:30.810 --> 23:33.960
<i>My song is a song of joy and wishes</i>

23:33.960 --> 23:36.660
<i>Yes, I try to reach out</i>

23:36.660 --> 23:41.820
<i>But you're too high up 
in the evening stars</i>
